                <pb facs="0553" n="481" xml:id="pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 15778/31.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon says the President appreciates the prompt action taken by the
                    Government of Panama and the determination to prevent further abuses by
                    punishing those guilty of misconduct. Says orders will be given to pursue the
                    usual course and also to keep a reserve ready to render assistance if necessary
                    for the preservation of order. Adds that the President feels it to be important
                    that action to determine the culpability of police officials charged, by
                    judicial investigation, decision, and punishment, should be taken without
                    delay.</p>
            </div>
